<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30325" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbătaea</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbăthaea</span></b> ),
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναβαταια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a country in Arabia Petræa</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 21,
				18, 72, § 120</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbă-thaeus</span></b>  (scanned
			Năbătaeus, Năbāthaeus,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 5, 284</span></i>), a,
				um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναβαθαῖος</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Nabathæa, Nabathœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saltus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 126</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbătaei</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbăthaei</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναβαταῖοι</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναβαθαῖοι</span>, <i>the
			Nabathæans</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 28, 32, § 144</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">12, 20, 44, §
				98</span></i>; Auct. B. Alex. 1, 1; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2,
			57</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 8,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Poet.</b>, transf., for <i>Arabian,
				Eastern, Oriental</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Eurus ad Auroram Nabathaeaque regna recessit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					1, 61</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nabathaei flatus Euri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc. 4,
					63</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Năbăthes</span></b> ,
				ae, m., <i>a
				Nabathæan</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet. 160</span></i>.</div>
